# Rydex Privacy Policy

**Last Updated: July 26, 2026**

This Privacy Policy explains how Rydex ("Rydex," "we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and protects information when you use the Rydex Discord bot (the "Service"). By inviting Rydex to a server or otherwise using the Service, you agree to the collection and use of information as described in this policy.

---

## 1. Information We Collect

Rydex is a Components V2 container-building bot. We only collect the data necessary to make the bot function.

### 1.1 Data You Provide Directly
- **Container content** — the text, layout, colors, image/thumbnail URLs, and button links you create using the container builder. This is content you choose to include; we do not inspect or moderate it beyond what is needed for the bot to function.
- **Discord identifiers** — your Discord user ID and username, where required to attribute or restrict actions (for example, author-only interaction locks, or no-prefix permission grants).

### 1.2 Data Collected Automatically
- **Server (guild) data** — guild ID and guild name, used to scope saved containers to the correct server and enforce per-server container name uniqueness.
- **Channel and message IDs** — recorded when a container is sent, so it can be tracked, edited, or referenced later.
- **Container data** — saved container names, layouts, and accent colors, stored per server so they can be recalled, edited, cloned, or listed later (e.g. via `container info`, `container clone`, `container list`).
- **Administrative/action logs** — for bot-owner and moderation tooling, we may log which action was performed, in which server, by whom, and when (e.g. granting no-prefix access, reboots). This is limited to operational/administrative actions, not general user messages.
- **Basic technical/telemetry data** — uptime, latency, and system resource usage used for the bot's internal status dashboard. This data is aggregate and not tied to individual users.

### 1.3 What We Do Not Collect
- We do **not** read, log, or store the general content of your messages outside of the container-builder flow.
- We do **not** collect presence data (online/offline/idle status).
- We do **not** collect payment information — Rydex is free to use.
- We do **not** knowingly collect data from users under the age of 13 (or the minimum age required by Discord's Terms of Service in your jurisdiction, if higher).

---

## 2. Discord Permissions & Intents

To operate, Rydex requests the following privileged intents from Discord:
- **Server Members Intent** — used to identify users for permission checks (e.g. author-only controls, owner/no-prefix access).
- **Message Content Intent** — used to read command invocations (e.g. `.container`, `.help`) so the bot can respond to prefix commands.

We only use these intents for the purposes described above and do not use them for bulk data harvesting.

---

## 3. How We Use Information

We use the information we collect to:
- Provide, operate, and maintain the container builder and related bot features
- Save, edit, duplicate, list, and send containers on your behalf, per server
- Enforce Discord's component and rate limits to keep the Service functional
- Restrict certain commands to authorized users (e.g. the command author, server admins, or bot owners)
- Diagnose bugs, monitor bot health, and improve performance
- Maintain administrative logs for accountability of owner-level actions

We do not sell your data. We do not use your data for advertising or share it with third parties for marketing purposes.

---

## 4. Data Storage & Retention

- Container data, button actions, and sent-container records are stored in a database tied to the relevant server (guild) ID and persist until you delete them, the container is removed via a bot command, or Rydex is removed from your server.
- If Rydex is removed from a server, associated container data for that server may be deleted during routine cleanup, though this is not guaranteed to happen immediately.
- Administrative logs (e.g. no-prefix grants, owner action logs) are retained for as long as reasonably necessary for accountability and abuse-prevention purposes.
- We take reasonable technical measures to protect stored data but cannot guarantee absolute security, as no method of electronic storage is 100% secure.

---

## 5. Data Sharing

We do not share, sell, or rent your information to third parties, except:
- Where required by law, legal process, or governmental request
- To protect the rights, property, or safety of Rydex, its users, or the public
- With Discord itself, as an inherent part of how the Service operates on Discord's platform (see [Discord's Privacy Policy](https://discord.com/privacy))

---

## 6. Your Rights & Choices

You may:
- Delete container data you created via the bot's own commands (e.g. removing/clearing a container)
- Request removal of data associated with your user ID by contacting us (see Section 9)
- Remove Rydex from your server at any time via Discord's server settings, which stops further data collection from that server

Since Rydex primarily stores data at the server (guild) level rather than tied to individual users, some data (e.g. shared container layouts) is managed collectively by server administrators.

---

## 7. Children's Privacy

Rydex is not directed at children under 13. Discord itself requires users to meet a minimum age to use its platform; please refer to [Discord's Terms of Service](https://discord.com/terms) for details. If we become aware that we have inadvertently collected data from a user below the applicable minimum age, we will delete it.

